chapters/01-cell-file.html:60:<p>The opening offer is a two-stage paid diagnostic for one cell already installed but not finally accepted. Stage one is a desk review at a <strong>€1,250 design hurdle</strong>, credited against stage two. It checks scope, declarations, drawings, risk logic and planned tests. Stage two is the site challenge and evidence pack at a <strong>€4,500 total design hurdle</strong>. The integrator pays 50% before the desk review and the balance before the site date.</p>
chapters/01-cell-file.html:63:<p>The online record does not settle the pitch's kill fact. IAB publishes €6,000 for CE work on a simple machine and about €30,000 for a machinery assembly, both including a manual. <!-- CHECK: 01-incumbent-price --> Those are broad anchors, not cobot-cell quotes. The named Dutch integrator and safety-bureau pages reviewed here publish scope but no cell-file price. <!-- CHECK: 01-price-boundary --> The record therefore cannot exclude a dealer bundling the work or a competent bureau quoting below €3,000.</p>
chapters/01-cell-file.html:72:<tr><td><strong>Year 1 alongside the job:</strong> six cell challenges and six modification screens.</td><td>6 × €4.5k plus 6 × €1k. <strong>Total €33k.</strong></td><td>Contract safety review €5k; instrument rental and calibration allowance €2k; travel and Dutch document support €2k. <strong>Gross margin €24k (73%).</strong></td><td>Founder delivery at a €27k replacement-cost hurdle plus €8k insurance, training, standards, sales and admin leaves <strong>−€11k</strong>. No owner income.</td></tr>
chapters/01-cell-file.html:73:<tr><td><strong>Mature design:</strong> fifty cell challenges and twenty-five modification screens.</td><td>50 × €5.5k plus 25 × €1.25k. <strong>Total €306k.</strong></td><td>One delivery engineer, loaded, €85k; contract senior review €20k; instruments €12k; language and travel €10k. <strong>Gross margin €179k (59%).</strong></td><td>Founder replacement cost €100k plus €45k insurance, standards, sales and admin leaves <strong>€34k</strong> before tax and financing.</td></tr>
chapters/01-cell-file.html:77:<p>Gross margin pays the delivery engineer, contract review, instruments, language support and travel. Founder replacement is below gross margin, as owner compensation rather than free labour. The €34,000 remainder is company surplus, not additional salary. It must absorb variance, claims, sick time and investment.</p>
chapters/01-cell-file.html:78:<p>Working capital is light only if the boundary holds. Bill 50% in advance, rent the measurement kit until ten paid site jobs, and make the integrator buy any guards, sensors or redesign. The <strong>year-one cash-at-risk hurdle is €15,000</strong>: up to €4,500 before evidence, then training, insurance advice, standards access, rental deposits and travel from receipts. Do not buy a cell, van or permanent test kit to create demand.</p>
chapters/01-cell-file.html:111:<li><strong>Days 30–60:</strong> offer the €1,250 desk diagnostic to five qualified integrators, 50% in advance. Credit it into the €4,500 site challenge. The partner must name the manufacturer, cell, acceptance date and Dutch interview lead.</li>
chapters/01-cell-file.html:113:<li><strong>Days 76–90:</strong> offer the same scope to a second integrator and ask the first for a second cell at the mature €5,500 hurdle. Total spend before the first paid diagnostic is capped at <strong>€4,500</strong>.</li>
chapters/01-cell-file.html:115:<p><strong>Pass:</strong> two integrators buy desk diagnostics, one converts to a paid site challenge, and one offers a second cell at the mature price. The partner owns Dutch instructions and the final declaration. Delivery shows a route to fewer than two founder days per repeat cell. <strong>Kill:</strong> five qualified offers produce no paid diagnostic; any credible provider quotes a complete comparable cell file below €3,000; all five integrators bundle validation internally; or every buyer requires the entrant to lead Dutch operator interviews. The national installation count is not a pass criterion. Payment through two channels is better evidence.</p>

